<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anne of Cleves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1515–1557</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> was a daughter of Duke John III of Cleves and the fourth wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII of England</a>. The marriage, arranged in 1540 to ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> with the Protestant-leaning princes of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, was annulled after six months. She remained in England with a generous settlement and outlived the king's other wives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves.jpg" alt="Anne of Cleves" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Holbein the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anne_de_Cl%C3%A8ves_-_Hans_Holbein_le_Jeune_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_INV_1348_;_MR_756_-_version_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
